To create a custom input action for a XR origin that allows the user to activate the pause function, we will need to follow the steps outlined below:

1. Create a new C# script in Unity and name it "PauseInputAction".
2. Define the input action in the Awake() method:
```csharp
public override void Awake()
{
    // Get the XR origin component of the game object.
    XROrigin origin = GetComponent<XROrigin>();

    // Register the input action.
    origin.InputActionathing += OnInputAction;
}
```
3. Define the OnInputAction method to handle the input action:
```csharp
private void OnInputAction(InputAction.CallbackContext context)
{
    // Check if the input action is the one we want to listen to.
    if (context.InputAction.Name == "PauseInputAction")
    {
        // Get the XR origin component of the game object.
        XROrigin origin = GetComponent<XROrigin>();

        // Pause the simulation.
        origin.Pause();
    }
}
```
4. Attach the PauseInputAction script to the game object that you want to use as the XR origin.

This script will listen for the "PauseInputAction" input action, and when triggered, it will pause the XR origin's simulation.

Note: This is just one possible solution, and there may be other solutions that are also suitable depending on your specific requirements and constraints. It is important to carefully consider the design of your system and to choose the solution that is best suited to your needs.

